From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] luma: keep the live island's indicator inside it

The event island turned into an empty slab beside the clock: material
and padding, nothing within. The instrumentation measured it exactly --
natural=0, content.w=1, island=21 -- so the island's content had no
children, and the scroll viewport clamped itself to the one pixel its
floor allows.

The indicator's container was only ever inserted into the island at the
moment the island was first built. Rebuilding the panel, which a monitor
or scale change does, hands that container back to the panel, and
nothing put it back. Every neighbouring actor in the same function is
already re-parented idempotently on each sync; this one now is too.

diff --git a/js/ui/shelf.js b/js/ui/shelf.js
--- a/js/ui/shelf.js
+++ b/js/ui/shelf.js
@@ -598,9 +598,7 @@
         const live = liveIndicator?.container;
         if (live) {
             if (!this._liveIsland) {
-                live.get_parent()?.remove_child(live);
                 this._liveContent = new St.BoxLayout();
-                this._liveContent.add_child(live);
                 this._liveScroll = new St.ScrollView({
                     enable_mouse_scrolling: true,
                     overlay_scrollbars: true,
@@ -616,6 +614,17 @@
                     this._queueDockWidth();
                 }, this);
             }
+            // Every other adopted actor is re-parented on each sync; this
+            // one was only ever put in place when the island was first built.
+            // Rebuilding the panel -- which a monitor or scale change does --
+            // hands the indicator's container back to the panel, and the
+            // island was then left holding nothing at all: it kept its
+            // material and its padding, measured zero, and drew as an empty
+            // slab beside the clock with the event nowhere to be seen.
+            if (live.get_parent() !== this._liveContent) {
+                live.get_parent()?.remove_child(live);
+                this._liveContent.add_child(live);
+            }
             if (this._liveIsland.get_parent() !== this._group) {
                 this._liveIsland.get_parent()?.remove_child(this._liveIsland);
                 this._group.insert_child_at_index(this._liveIsland, 1);
